            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0513" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Detention/54</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Téllez</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-15">April 15, 1929</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2180</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of Your Excellency’s kind note of April 5 of this year, in which you
                    were so good as to inform me that instructions were duly given to the
                    appropriate authorities of the American Army to permit the return to Mexican
                    territory of the Mexican Federal officer and of the ten soldiers who were
                    arrested by the local authorities of Naco, Arizona, on April 3.</p>
                <p>Your Excellency was good enough also to declare to me that the arms and munitions
                    which were in the possession of the said soldiers will be kept for the present
                    by the American authorities and later returned to the Mexican Federal Commandant
                    of Naco, Sonora.</p>
                <p>I am happy to inform Your Excellency that the necessary orders will be duly given
                    with a view to preventing Mexican soldiers from crossing the dividing line in
                    the future.</p>
                <p>Thanking Your Excellency most sincerely for the attention you were so kind as to
                    give this matter, I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel C. Téllez</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
